WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.850
I'M HERE TO PRESENT THE OSCAR
FOR BEST ACTRESS.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:07.360
THE ACADEMY HAS RECOGNIZED SOME
OUTSTANDING PERFORMANCES THIS YEAR.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.360
25 YEARS AGO SHE MADE HER BROADWAY
DEBUT IN AN AUGUST WILSON PLAY.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.260
TONIGHT, VIOLA DAVIS IS
NOMINATED FOR BRINGING TO LIFE

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.690
ANOTHER OF THAT GREAT AMERICAN
PLAYWRIGHT'S WORK, AS THE LEAD

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:22.449
ACTRESS IN "MA RAINEY'S BLACK
BOTTOM."

00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:25.310
YOU WERE LUMINOUS IN THAT ROLE,
VIOLA.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:30.100
ANDRA DAY, IT'S HARD TO BELIEVE
"THE UNITED STATES VS. BILLIE HOLIDAY"

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.160
IS YOUR FIRST MAJOR FILM ROLE.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.130
YOU SEAMLESSLY EMBODIED THE
ICON, AND REMINDED US THAT

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.789
BILLIE HOLIDAY WAS A SURVIVOR
AND A FIGHTER.

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:41.760
VANESSA KIRBY, YOU WENT THERE
FOR YOUR PERFORMANCE IN

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.960
"PIECES OF A WOMAN."

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.280
WHICH IS WHY YOUR PEERS HAVE

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.379
RECOGNIZED THIS FEARLESS AND
VULNERABLE PERFORMANCE.

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:51.949
FRANCES MCDORMAND, IN THIS
UNTETHERED MOMENT, WE NEEDED

00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:54.239
YOUR PERFORMANCE IN "NOMADLAND."

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:55.899
YOU TOOK US INTO A WORLD HIDING

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:00.219
IN PLAIN SIGHT WITH CHARISMA AND
TRANSPARENCY.

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:03.199
CAREY MULLIGAN, YOU KNEW THE
RISK YOU WERE TAKING WITH

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:04.570
"PROMISING YOUNG WOMAN."

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.180
CONGRATULATIONS ON A PERFORMANCE

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.550
THAT WAS PAINFUL, WITTY, AND
POWERFUL.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:14.790
AND THE BEST OSCAR FOR BEST
ACTRESS GOES TO --

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.460
FRANCES MCDORMAND, "NOMADLAND."

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:35.979
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:36.979
♪

00:01:42.474 --> 00:01:43.480
LOOK, THEY DIDN'T ASK ME.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:47.570
BUT IF THEY HAD, I WOULD HAVE
SAID, KARAOKE. BECAUSE,

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:52.170
WHEN YOU HAVE VOICES LIKE LESLIE
AND MARCUS AND -- WE SHOULD ADD

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.072
A KARAOKE BAR.

00:01:53.072 --> 00:01:54.271
OKAY?

00:01:55.924 --> 00:01:58.814
I HAVE NO WORDS.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:02.250
MY VOICE IS IN MY SWORD.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:07.833
WE KNOW THE SWORD IS OUR WORK.

00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:10.342
AND I LIKE WORK.

00:02:10.342 --> 00:02:11.969
THANK YOU FOR KNOWING THAT.

00:02:11.969 --> 00:02:13.170
AND THANKS FOR THIS.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.083
[ APPLAUSE ]

